-- 200_sh4_recompiler_lane.surql -- the SH4 RECOMPILER lane, 2026-09-07: the NAOMI cart frame tick
-- located and paired with the DC tick, the relink-delta reality (there is no single code delta), the
-- cart header, Ghidra SH4 p-code lowering coverage, the two export landmines (delay-slot folding,
-- p-code-relative branch const size 4), the GATE S1 harness asymmetry, and the pointer to the
-- already byte-exact SH4 executor so a KB reader finds it BEFORE building a second one.
--
-- RE METHOD: reference = the annotated marvelous2 SH4 disassembly (DC 1ST_READ.BIN, base 0x8C010000);
-- target = the NAOMI cart epr-23085a.ic11 program image (base 0x0C021000). Matching is by unique
-- constant / instruction-stream fingerprint, never by instruction bytes or by relocated addresses.
-- Requested as 178_sh4_recompiler_lane.surql; renumbered to 200 because 178_arc_residency_afs.surql
-- already exists and a duplicate NN would shadow it in every seed-NNN citation.
-- Forward slashes only in ref/note; no apostrophes (a backslash in a single-quoted string is an
-- invalid escape, the request returns HTTP 400, and the whole file is discarded).
USE NS re DB kb;

-- ============================ SOURCES ============================

UPSERT source:sh4_recompiler_lane_20260907 SET kind='disasm', strength='code',
  ref='Reference side: maplecast-flycast/refs/marvelous2/bank03.asm lines 13272-13340 (loc_8c03589a, loc_8c0358be, literal pool loc_8c0359f0..loc_8c035a14) and work.asm line 1 (#symbol GameGlobalPointer 0x8c26823c). Target side: the NAOMI cart program image naomi_prog.bin (rom epr-23085a.ic11 + 0x1000, 0x250000 bytes, base 0x0C021000) analysed in a headless Ghidra SuperH4:LE:32:default project, exported with PcodeExportAll.java (ALL = every instruction in the analysed listing) to naomi_pcode.jsonl, plus FuncDump.java per-function mnHash/mnOpHash to dc_funcs.tsv (4169 functions) and naomi_funcs.tsv (4677 functions).',
  note='Scratchpad session e0483024 sh4/. All NAOMI addresses are cart RAM addresses; file offset in naomi_prog.bin = addr - 0x0C021000, and file offset in epr-23085a.ic11 = addr - 0x0C021000 + 0x1000.';

UPSERT source:naomi_cart_epr23085a SET kind='capture', strength='reproduction',
  ref='epr-23085a.ic11, 4194304 bytes. Header read directly: magic at 0x00, publisher at 0x10, eight 32-byte region titles at 0x30, build date and serial at 0x130, main load descriptor at 0x360, test load descriptor at 0x3C0, entry points and region/player bytes at 0x420. Test-mode strings read at 0x3EE0C0..0x3EE4C0.',
  note='This is the users own arcade cart dump. BYOR: no ROM-derived bytes are committed anywhere; only addresses, sizes and header field values are recorded here.';

UPSERT source:sh4_pcode_measurements_20260907 SET kind='capture', strength='reproduction',
  ref='Re-measured on 2026-09-07 from sh4/naomi_pcode.jsonl (cart, 836479 records, 0 export errors), sh4/sh4_pcode_real.jsonl (DC, 29702 records of which 23697 carry real=true meaning they came from the ANALYSED listing, 4252 PseudoDisassembler fallback, 1753 null) and sh4/sh4_pcode.jsonl (the same DC address list exported through PseudoDisassembler only).',
  note='Every number in the findings below was recomputed from these files in this pass rather than quoted from the earlier report; two quoted numbers did not reproduce and are recorded as retracted.';

UPSERT source:gate_s1_lift_run_20260907 SET kind='capture', strength='reproduction',
  ref='sh4/pcode2c.py emitter + sh4/lift_rt.h runtime + sh4/s1_host.c harness vs sh4/s1_pcode.py, an independently written p-code interpreter. Run A = DC function 0x8c1236e0 (32 instructions) -> outA/c.txt and outA/p.txt. Run B = DC function 0x8c0322d6 (36 records, 34 after the delay-slot drop) -> outB/c.txt and outB/p.txt.',
  note='Run A: C and the oracle agree exactly on the return value 0xdeadbeef and on all ten dumped registers (r0-r7, r14, r15), oracle steps = 32. Run B: the oracle terminates with interpreter step limit and the C side produced no output. GATE S1 is therefore PASSED for one function and OPEN for the second.';

UPSERT source:sh4_executor_handoff_20260720 SET kind='doc', strength='reproduction',
  ref='maplecast-flycast/tools/render-replica-poc/HANDOFF-EXECUTOR.md (last updated 2026-07-20, branch feat/dataset-exporter, exec commit 4f93dc647), sections 1-9: the transpile pipeline, the memory model in sh4ctx.h (mc_is_ram area-3 gate), the verification stack (verify_leaf.c, realcore runner --leaf oracle, test_tick.c whole-tick diff masking 0x8C2D5748 / 0x8C32DBAC / 0x8C268250), the fix changelog and the 52-byte root cause.',
  note='The doc records a REPRODUCTION, not an opinion: the transpiled tick diffs 0 bytes over the full 16 MB RAM image against flycast, seeded at 0x8C0358BE. Companion findings already in the graph: executor_tick_byte_exact, sh4_area3_write_gate, sh4_delay_slot_latch, executor_sh4_handback_open.';

-- ============================ THE PAIR ============================

UPSERT finding:naomi_frame_tick_located SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='The NAOMI cart frame tick is 0x0C02AB2C, 18 instructions, instruction-for-instruction identical to the DC tick loc_8c03589a, and its scene-FSM callee 0x0C02AB50 pairs with DC loc_8c0358be',
  statement='naomi_frame_tick = 0x0C02AB2C .. 0x0C02AB4E, 18 instructions / 36 bytes: mov.l 0x0c02ac74,r2 (globals pointer literal) ; mov #0x1a,r0 ; sts.l PR,@-r15 ; mov.l @r2,r3 ; mov.b @(r0,r3),r1 ; tst r1,r1 ; bf 0x0c02ab3e ; bsr 0x0c02ab50 ; _nop ; mov.l 0x0c02ac74,r1 ; mov #0x1a,r2 ; mov #0x0,r3 ; mov.l @r1,r0 ; add r0,r2 ; mov.b r3,@r2 ; mov.l 0x0c02ac78,r3 ; jmp @r3 ; _lds.l @r15+,PR. The DC twin loc_8c03589a (bank03.asm:13272) is the same 18 instructions in the same order with the same operands; Ghidra records it as FUN_8c03589a, 18 instructions, 36 bytes, mnHash b53be7184a6e46eab32b6c163a268a3bbbe71646, mnOpHash 21dc86768227e2467064cda727de916e83a1ff86. Shape: load the globals pointer, read the byte at GameGlobal+0x1A (the vblank request flag), tst, bf past the body, bsr the scene FSM, then re-load the globals pointer and store 0 back to GameGlobal+0x1A, then tail-jmp through the literal at 0x0C02AC78 = 0x0C028B24 (DC loc_8c0338ec). naomi_scene_fsm = 0x0C02AB50 (DC loc_8c0358be, bank03.asm:13295): the first 27 mnemonics are identical, then the builds diverge -- at instruction 28 the DC build has a four-instruction gate the cart does NOT have (mov.l @(loc_8c035a10,PC),r3 ; mov.b @r3,r1 ; tst r1,r1 ; bf loc_8c035916, reading the byte at 0x8C213046) before the frame-counter update, whereas the cart goes straight to mov.l @(0x1c,r1),r3 ; add #0x1,r3. The state dispatch itself (mov.l @r14,r3 ; mov.l table,r0 ; mov.b @r3,r2 ; shll2 r2 ; mov.l @(r0,r2),r3 ; jsr @r3) is INSIDE the identical prefix; only the table CONTENTS differ (cart table 0x0C23A9A4, DC table bank14.loc_8c14d1a4 = 0x8C14D1A4).',
  consequence='The cart has a frame tick with the same contract as the DC one: it is gated on a vblank byte at GameGlobal+0x1A, it clears that byte, and everything the frame does happens under one bsr. That is the same shape as the Steam recompile pair FUN_140118950 / FUN_140607D60, so the three builds can be reasoned about as one function under three relinks.',
  caveat='Located statically. Nothing has been RUN on the cart image; the tick has not been ticked. The gate for that is unchanged and is not that it disassembles: a cart tick would have to reproduce a state the cart itself produced.';

UPSERT finding:instruction_stream_search_beats_boundary_hashing SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='METHOD: when two builds are relinked, slide the reference mnemonic sequence over the whole analysed instruction stream of the target -- function-boundary hashing misses whatever the target analysis never made a function',
  statement='Sliding the 18-mnemonic tick sequence over all 836479 analysed cart instructions returns EXACTLY ONE match, at 0x0C02AB2C (re-run and reproduced in this pass). Function-boundary hashing could not find it for a specific, measurable reason: the NAOMI Ghidra analysis produced NO FUNCTION whose body contains 0x0C02AB2C at all, so the function did not exist to be hashed. Boundary hashing is not useless in general on this pair -- across 4169 DC and 4677 NAOMI functions, 2050 mnHash values and 2079 mnOpHash values intersect -- it simply cannot see a routine the target analysis never bounded. The instruction-stream slide has no such dependency; it needs only that the target listing be disassembled.',
  consequence='Standing rule for cross-build matching on relinked images: run BOTH. Use per-function mnHash/mnOpHash (FuncDump.java) for the bulk pairing, and fall back to a raw mnemonic-sequence slide for any specific routine the hash pass does not answer. Mnemonic sequences survive relinking because they contain no addresses; a length-18 sequence was already unique in 836k instructions.',
  caveat='The slide is a mnemonic-only comparison, so it would also match a genuinely different routine that happened to share the sequence. Uniqueness in this corpus (1 hit) plus operand-level agreement against bank03.asm is what makes the identification safe, not the slide alone.';

-- ============================ THE RELINK DELTAS (CORRECTION) ============================

UPSERT finding:dc_naomi_relink_is_not_a_constant_delta SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='CORRECTION: there is NO single DC-minus-NAOMI code delta. 0x8000AD6E holds only for the tick pair; five other code pointers in the very same literal pool give five different deltas. The work-RAM data delta 0x7FF912B8 does hold, on two independent samples, but not for image-resident data',
  statement='Every literal in the tick and scene-FSM pool was resolved on both sides and differenced (DC minus NAOMI, mod 2^32). CODE: tick entry 0x8C03589A vs 0x0C02AB2C = 0x8000AD6E; scene FSM 0x8C0358BE vs 0x0C02AB50 = 0x8000AD6E -- but these two are NOT independent, they are 0x24 apart in both builds so an equal delta is arithmetically forced. The genuinely independent code pointers in the same pool disagree: loc_8c0338ec vs 0x0C028B24 = 0x8000ADC8; loc_8c0395a0 vs 0x0C02C308 = 0x8000D298; loc_8c030f54 vs 0x0C0268E8 = 0x8000A66C; loc_8c02dc4c vs 0x0C023688 = 0x8000A5C4; loc_8c0355c2 vs 0x0C02A7FA = 0x8000ADC8. Spread across those five is about 0x2CD4, i.e. the two images have different internal layouts (the DC 1ST_READ.BIN is 1809817 bytes, the cart program is 2424832 bytes), so the relink is per-function, not a shift. DATA: GameGlobalPointer 0x8C26823C vs 0x0C2D6F84 = 0x7FF912B8 and the flag pointer 0x8C2152CC vs 0x0C284014 = 0x7FF912B8 -- two independent work-RAM globals 0x52F70 apart, same delta. But the state dispatch TABLE 0x8C14D1A4 vs 0x0C23A9A4 = 0x7FF12800, a third value: that table is image-resident on DC, not a work-RAM global. Also noted: 0x7FF912B8 is the same constant previously observed as an S_PLxx overlay delta, which is independent corroboration for the work-RAM band.',
  consequence='Carrying DC RE to the cart is NOT two subtractions. Exactly one band is currently known to translate by a constant: DC work-RAM globals in the 0x8C21xxxx..0x8C26xxxx range map to cart addresses by subtracting 0x7FF912B8 (two samples). Code addresses and image-resident data must be re-matched per routine, by fingerprint. Anyone who applies 0x8000AD6E as a general code delta will land on the wrong function almost everywhere.',
  caveat='The work-RAM delta rests on TWO samples. What would confirm it: resolve ten more paired work-RAM literals from other identical-prefix routines and check they all give 0x7FF912B8, and find the boundary addresses where it stops holding. The per-function code relink is CONFIRMED (five counterexamples) rather than inferred.';

-- ============================ THE CART HEADER ============================

UPSERT finding:naomi_cart_header_epr23085a SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  title='NAOMI cart header of epr-23085a.ic11, read field by field: magic NAOMI, publisher CAPCOM.,LTD., eight region titles, build date 2000-02-25, serial BBG0, main load rom+0x1000 -> 0x0C021000 for 2424832 bytes, entry 0x0C021000, test entry 0x0C020000',
  statement='Offsets are file offsets in epr-23085a.ic11 (4194304 bytes). 0x00 magic NAOMI (16 bytes, space padded). 0x10 publisher CAPCOM.,LTD. (32 bytes). 0x30 eight 32-byte titles: MARVEL VS CAPCOM2 JAPAN / USA / EXPORT / KOREA / AUSTRALIA then three unqualified. 0x130 build date as little-endian u16 year 0x07D0 = 2000 then u8 month 0x02 then u8 day 0x19 = 25, so 2000-02-25. 0x134 serial BBG0 (4 ASCII). Main load descriptor at 0x360: rom offset 0x00001000, destination 0x0C021000, length 0x00250000 = 2424832, terminator 0xFFFFFFFF -- exactly ONE entry. Test-mode load descriptor at 0x3C0: rom offset 0x003C0000, destination 0x0C020000, length 0x00040000, terminator 0xFFFFFFFF -- also one entry. 0x420 game entry 0x0C021000; 0x424 test entry 0x0C020000; 0x428 = 0xFF; 0x429 = 0x02; then 0x00 0x01 0x00 0xFF 0x03 0x00.',
  consequence='The whole cart program is one flat 0x250000 image at a fixed base with no ASLR and no overlays in the header, so file offset in the program image = addr - 0x0C021000 and file offset in the rom = addr - 0x0C021000 + 0x1000. That is what makes a static lift of the cart tractable at all.',
  caveat='The interpretation of 0x428 as a supported-region bitmask (0xFF = all) and 0x429 as the supported player count (2) follows the public NAOMI header layout, not anything in this file -- the BYTES are CONFIRMED, the NAMES are INFERRED. The part number BBGH09A0 does NOT appear anywhere in epr-23085a.ic11 (the only BBG match in all 4 MB is the serial BBG0 at 0x134); it is external cataloguing metadata and is recorded here as NOT read from the rom.';

UPSERT finding:naomi_arcade_game_config_menu SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  title='The arcade GAME CONFIGRATION menu strings are in the cart at file offset 0x3EE2F0: SOUND MODE, DEMO SOUND HALF, CONTINUE, VOICE TYPE, DIFFICULTY, DAMAGE LEVEL, TIMER SPEED, VM-KIT TYPE, VM WRITE, GAME SPEED, EVENT, JOIN-IN, DEFAULT, SAVE and EXIT -- with the value strings, including NORMAL and TURBO, at 0x3EE118',
  statement='epr-23085a.ic11 file offsets. Label block from 0x3EE2F0: GAME CONFIGRATION (spelled without the U in the rom), then SOUND MODE, DEMO SOUND HALF, CONTINUE, VOICE TYPE, DIFFICULTY, DAMAGE LEVEL, TIMER SPEED, VM-KIT TYPE, VM WRITE, GAME SPEED, EVENT, JOIN-IN, DEFAULT, SAVE and EXIT, followed by the help lines SELECT OPTION = 1P UP or DOWN and MODIFY SETTING = 1P LEFT or RIGHT. Value block from 0x3EE0C0: STEREO, OFF, ON, EASY[...]HARD, LOW[...]HIGH, NO USE, SEGA, CAPCOM, then at 0x3EE118 FREE SELECT, NORMAL, TURBO, then SAVING NEW CONFIGURATION IN EEPROM. Preceding blocks are the TEST GAME DATA counters and the ROM BOARD TEST list IC17..IC32 64M. A second NORMAL / TURBO pair exists at 0x20D188 / 0x20D194 next to STAGE : %02X, which is the debug stage menu rather than the operator menu.',
  consequence='The arcade GAME SPEED option with its NORMAL / TURBO / FREE SELECT values is the same setting the Steam build exposes as descriptor row 3 -> config+0x298 -> G+0x49 (see finding:game_speed_config_and_block_fields). The arcade original stores it in EEPROM through the operator menu; the collection turned it into a per-match settings column. This is the cheapest available cross-check that a Steam setting is an original arcade setting rather than a port addition.',
  caveat='String presence only. Which option index maps to which config byte on the cart has NOT been traced; that needs the operator-menu writer routine.';

-- ============================ P-CODE LOWERING AND EMITTER COVERAGE ============================

UPSERT finding:sh4_pcode_lowering_coverage SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='Ghidra SuperH4:LE:32:default lowers this game essentially completely: the whole cart is 836479 instructions / 2163268 p-code operations with ZERO unimplemented and 87 CALLOTHER (99.996 percent of operations lowered); the DC analysed sample is 23697 instructions / 59564 operations with ONE CALLOTHER (99.9983 percent)',
  statement='Re-measured in this pass. CART (naomi_pcode.jsonl, PcodeExportAll ALL over the analysed listing): 836479 records, 0 export errors, 0 unimplemented, 2163268 p-code operations, 45 distinct opcodes, 12017 records with an empty op list (nop 3173, _nop 8651, pref 184, _pref 9 -- correct, those instructions have no p-code), 87 CALLOTHER by mnemonic: bsr 34, _mac.l 34, trapa 5, fsca 6, ocbp 4, ocbi 1, mac.l 1, _ocbwb 1, rts 1. 87 of 2163268 leaves 99.99598 percent of operations lowered. DC (sh4_pcode_real.jsonl restricted to the 23697 records marked real=true, i.e. taken from the analysed listing): 0 errors, 59564 operations, 43 distinct opcodes, 1 CALLOTHER (ocbp), leaving 99.99832 percent. The 45 cart opcodes are the ordinary integer / float / branch set plus INT_CARRY, INT_SRIGHT, TRUNC, FLOAT_SQRT, FLOAT_ABS -- no SIMD, no 80-bit or 128-bit varnodes.',
  consequence='The p-code path that already carried the Steam x86-64 frame function into C and into wasm needs NO architecture-specific work for SH4. The residual 87 CALLOTHER sites are cache-control (ocbi / ocbp / ocbwb), trapa, fsca and the mac.l accumulate idiom, all of which are individually implementable; none of them is a hole in the lifter.',
  caveat='Percentages are per p-code OPERATION, not per instruction. Both figures are for statically decoded instructions, not executed ones.';

UPSERT finding:trap_pseudodisassembler_hides_delay_slots SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='TRAP: measure and export SH4 p-code on the ANALYSED listing, never through PseudoDisassembler alone -- Ghidra folds the delay-slot instruction into the branch op list AND emits it again at pc+2, and only the analysed listing marks that second record with a leading underscore',
  statement='Ghidra SH4 semantics: for a delayed branch, the BRANCH instruction record already carries the delay-slot instruction operations inside its own op list, and a SECOND record exists at pc+2 carrying the same operations. Measured example in the cart: 0x0C0210FA bf/s 0x0C021108 has ops COPY, INT_ADD, INT_EQUAL, CBRANCH -- the INT_ADD is the slot add r3,r14 -- and 0x0C0210FC is a separate record _add with ops INT_ADD. Same on the DC side: 0x8C010562 jsr @r3 has ops COPY, COPY, COPY, LOAD, CALLIND where the LOAD is the slot mov.l @r2,r4, and the record at 0x8C010564 is _mov.l with ops LOAD. Any consumer that executes both records DOUBLE-EXECUTES the delay slot. The only reliable marker is the leading underscore on the pc+2 mnemonic, and that marker exists ONLY in the analysed listing: exporting the SAME 23697 DC addresses through PseudoDisassembler in isolation produces records that differ from the analysed listing in exactly 2043 cases, and all 2043 are the delay-slot records losing their underscore (pseudo mov vs real _mov 779, nop vs _nop 508, mov.l vs _mov.l 337, add vs _add 112, fmov.s 65, mov.b 60, and so on). The cart listing contains 70742 underscore records. Folding still happens under PseudoDisassembler, so an export built on it is silently wrong rather than visibly wrong.',
  consequence='Rule for the lift pipeline: export from the ANALYSED listing, and drop every record whose mnemonic starts with an underscore AT EXPORT time (naomi_closure.py does this; it dropped 8 of 76 records for the tick closure). A pc-driven consumer must also advance past the slot: the branch record length is 2, so a naive pc += len lands on the dropped address.',
  caveat='RETRACTED from the earlier report: the figure that PseudoDisassembler reports 166 UNIMPLEMENTED on the same DC addresses does NOT reproduce from these artifacts. Measured, PseudoDisassembler reports ZERO unimplemented on those addresses; its actual defect is the missing delay-slot marking on 2043 records. The conclusion (measure on the analysed listing) is unchanged; the number 166 should not be quoted.';

UPSERT finding:trap_pcode_relative_branch_const_size SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='LANDMINE: on SH4 every p-code-relative BRANCH/CBRANCH offset is a size-FOUR constant (188483 of them in the cart, no other size), so any consumer that sign-extends the offset as 8 bytes turns a backward intra-instruction branch into a huge forward one -- silently, and in BOTH the emitter and the oracle at once',
  statement='A p-code BRANCH or CBRANCH whose first input lives in the CONSTANT space is a jump relative to the OP INDEX inside the same instruction, not a code address. Measured on the cart: 188483 such operations, and the constant varnode size is 4 in every single one -- the distribution is exactly {4: 188483}. Both current consumers sign-extend at 8 bytes: pcode2c.py reljump does off = int(v,16) then if off >= 1 shifted left 63 subtract 1 shifted left 64, and s1_pcode.py does i += sext(int(a,16), 8). A negative offset encoded as a size-4 constant, for example 0xFFFFFFFE, passes neither test, so it becomes +4294967294; pcode2c.py then takes its j >= len(ops) branch and emits goto L_end, and the interpreter runs off the end of the op list. Neither reports an error. Because the SAME wrong sign extension is in the emitter and in the independently written oracle, the two AGREE while both are wrong -- this is a convergence trap of exactly the kind that has produced false wins on this project before.',
  consequence='Fix both consumers to sign-extend at the CONSTANT VARNODE SIZE, not at 8. Until that is done, no result from the SH4 lift over any instruction containing an intra-instruction backward p-code branch can be trusted, and agreement between pcode2c.py and s1_pcode.py is not evidence about those instructions.',
  caveat='It has not been established that any of the 188483 SH4 sites actually uses a NEGATIVE offset -- the trap is latent until one does. What would settle it: histogram the 188483 constants and count how many exceed 0x7FFFFFFF. That check is cheap and should be run before the next gate.';

UPSERT finding:pcode2c_is_architecture_neutral SET status='inferred', confidence='medium', date='2026-09-07',
  title='pcode2c.py needs no SH4-specific change: it has an emitter arm for all 45 distinct p-code opcodes the cart uses, and it addresses registers by register-space byte offset rather than by architecture register name',
  statement='All 45 distinct opcodes appearing in the 2163268 cart operations are named in pcode2c.py (the set difference is empty). The machine model in lift_rt.h is a flat register-space byte array m->r of LIFT_REGSPACE = 0x1800 bytes plus a unique-space array, with every varnode access an unaligned little-endian load or store of its declared size, so the SH4 register file needs no declaration -- the exporter already emits Ghidra register-space offsets and the emitter just indexes them. Guest memory goes through the GP(a) macro, which is the identity for a native build and a page table for the wasm build.',
  consequence='One emitter serves the Steam x86-64 frame function and the SH4 DC and NAOMI code. That is what makes a cart cartridge conceivable at all without a second toolchain.',
  caveat='This is opcode-NAME coverage plus one compiled function, not proof of semantic correctness per opcode. The emitter has been compiled and run over exactly ONE SH4 function (GATE S1 run A, 32 instructions) and it is subject to finding:trap_pcode_relative_branch_const_size. Status stays medium until a whole-function or whole-tick SH4 gate passes.';

-- ============================ CLOSURE, BOUNDARY, ANCHOR, HARNESS ============================

UPSERT finding:naomi_tick_static_closure_is_indirect SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  title='The NAOMI tick static direct-flow closure is only 76 instructions across 152 bytes with 2 direct call targets and SEVEN indirect sites -- the cart frame is reached almost entirely through jsr @rN and a state-dispatch table, so a static lift of it is a lift of the indirect target set, not of a call tree',
  statement='Walking fallthrough, jump, cjump and direct call transitively from 0x0C02AB2C reaches 76 of the 836479 cart instructions, spanning 0x0C02AB2C..0x0C02ABC4, with 2 distinct direct call targets, 0 CALLOTHER, and 7 indirect sites (all icall). After dropping the 8 delay-slot records the exportable list is 68 records. The tick tail itself is an indirect jmp @r3 through a literal, and the scene FSM dispatches the global state byte through mov.l @(r0,r2),r3 ; jsr @r3 against the table at 0x0C23A9A4.',
  consequence='A static NAOMI lift needs the indirect target set BEFORE it needs a better call-graph walker. The DC lane already solved this the other way round: the existing executor resolves indirects from a real execution trace and routes every jsr/jmp/bsr/braf through one call_addr dispatch over every basic-block address (see finding:executor_tick_byte_exact). Do that on the cart, not a static jump-table resolution.',
  caveat='A count of 7 icall holes is for the 76-instruction closure only; the true reachable set is orders of magnitude larger and is not enumerated.';

UPSERT finding:sh4_recompiler_hardware_boundary SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='The hardware boundary for an SH4 lift of this game is ONE predicate plus three masked values: main RAM is SH4 area 3 only, mc_is_ram(a) = (a and 0x1C000000) == 0x0C000000, every write outside it is DROPPED, and three TCNT0-derived words are masked in the comparison',
  statement='Established on the DC lane and already byte-exact there. (1) Address space: only area 3 is game RAM. mc_is_ram(a) = (a and 0x1C000000) == 0x0C000000. VRAM, TA and MMIO writes must be DROPPED rather than aliased into the RAM array -- aliasing them let a texture-upload memcpy corrupt game RAM, and closing this took the whole-tick diff from 25565 bytes to 2612 (finding:sh4_area3_write_gate). (2) Time: exactly three TCNT0-derived words are masked in the whole-tick comparison, 0x8C2D5748, 0x8C32DBAC and 0x8C268250, proven non-cascading, plus the 0x8CFExxxx scratch stack (finding:executor_tick_byte_exact). (3) Peripherals: exactly one runtime target left the RAM domain, 0x89889011, read as a function pointer from the jump table at 0x8C1C95BC by loc_8c17D0C0; it is a non-RAM area-2 peripheral dispatch, dropped by mc_is_ram, and proven benign because full game RAM stays byte-exact with it dropped. (4) SH4 CPU semantics that are NOT optional: the delay-slot LATCH for register-indirect branches (finding:sh4_delay_slot_latch, diff 2612 to 113) and SZ-aware fmov into the FP back bank (diff 113 to 52). The NAOMI cart shares the SH4 and the same area-3 base, so the same predicate applies unchanged; the cart adds arcade-only peripherals (JVS input, EEPROM operator settings) which are outside area 3 and therefore already on the drop side of the predicate.',
  consequence='This is the SH4 lane analogue of finding:supergun_load_host_boundary: an ENUMERATED boundary, not something to rediscover one crash at a time. A lift that implements area-3-only memory, latches indirect branch targets, gets SZ-aware fmov right and masks the three timer words has no further hardware dependency for the game-logic tick.',
  caveat='Every item is DC-measured. Applying it to the cart is INFERRED until a cart tick is run: the arcade build reads JVS and EEPROM where the console build reads Maple and VMU, so the identity of the peripheral reads differs even though they all fall outside area 3.';

UPSERT finding:dc_input_dec_anchor SET status='inferred', confidence='medium', date='2026-09-07',
  title='Input_DEC 0x8C2681DC, stride 0x14, is the DC-side seat-word anchor (the decoded input the game acted on); the structural twin-call search for its NAOMI counterpart returned NOTHING, so the cart anchor is UNKNOWN',
  statement='DC: Input_DEC = 0x8C2681DC, both slots, stride 0x14 -- the semantic decoded input rather than the raw pad (maplecast-flycast/docs/DATASET-EXPORTER-DESIGN.md lines 50 and 154; the constant is loaded PC-relative all over the disassembly, for example marvelous2/build/bank01.asm lines 95, 117, 173 and as pool data at bank01:254 and bank03:7305). The structural signature used to look for it on the cart was: the main loop calls ONE routine TWICE within 0x40 bytes with two r4 constants exactly 0x14 apart. Run over all 836479 cart instructions (1060 mov.l literal to r4 sites with a resolvable constant, 4985 direct calls) this returned ZERO candidates with a 0x14 delta; widening to 0x10..0x20 produced five unrelated pairs (the 0x0C1CEDDA and 0x0C226A88 families, deltas 0x18 / 0x10 / 0x20). The tick was found by the mnemonic slide instead, not by this anchor.',
  consequence='The Input_DEC twin-call heuristic is recorded as a NEGATIVE result on the cart so nobody spends another pass on it. The cart input path must be found some other way -- most directly by pairing forward from the now-known scene FSM 0x0C02AB50.',
  caveat='Two open items. First, the naive prediction that cart Input_DEC = 0x8C2681DC - 0x7FF912B8 = 0x0C2D6F24 is UNVERIFIED and rests on a two-sample delta. Second, the DC-to-Steam correspondence does not close cleanly: under the block map G = blk+0x3CB8 maps to 0x8C268240, so 0x8C2681DC maps to blk+0x3C54, while the Steam decoded-input array is blk+0x3C66 -- the same 0x14 stride but 0x12 apart. Those are either two different arrays or the same array read at a different field. Do not treat blk+0x3C66 and Input_DEC as a confirmed pair until a set-site on both sides says so.';

UPSERT finding:trap_gate_s1_harness_asymmetry SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='TRAP: GATE S1 passed for one function while the C harness and the Python oracle were NOT the same machine -- the oracle masks every guest address into the 1 MB scratch, the C side computes an unchecked pointer, so the two only agree while the test stays in range',
  statement='GATE S1 lifts one SH4 function to C (pcode2c.py + lift_rt.h + s1_host.c) and compares it against s1_pcode.py, an interpreter written independently from the p-code spec, from an identical deterministic scratch fill. Run A, DC function 0x8c1236e0, 32 instructions: the two agree exactly -- return 0xdeadbeef and all ten dumped registers identical, oracle 32 steps. But the machines differ outside the scratch: s1_pcode.py load and store do o = addr and (SCRATCH_SZ - 1), so every guest address is legal, while the C side gets GP(a) = s1_scratch + (a - 0x0D000000) with NO mask, so an out-of-range guest address is unchecked pointer arithmetic into a 1 MB buffer. An earlier revision of the oracle asserted instead of masking, and the recorded failure is exactly that: s1out/p.txt ends with AssertionError guest load out of scratch: 0xe89346be while the C side produced no output at all. Run B, DC function 0x8c0322d6 (36 exported records, 34 after the delay-slot drop), does not agree: the oracle terminates with interpreter step limit at 200000 steps and the C side wrote nothing.',
  consequence='GATE S1 is PASSED for one function and OPEN for the second, and the pass is weaker than it reads because the two sides only coincide inside the scratch window. Fix before quoting S1 again: give both sides the SAME out-of-range policy (mask on both, or trap on both), and root-cause run B rather than dropping it.',
  caveat='This finding is about the harness, not about the emitter. It says nothing about whether pcode2c.py is correct; it says the current gate cannot tell. It compounds with finding:trap_pcode_relative_branch_const_size, where both sides are wrong in the same way.';

UPSERT finding:sh4_lane_entry_point SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='READ FIRST for any SH4 work: a byte-exact SH4 game-tick executor ALREADY EXISTS. maplecast-flycast/tools/render-replica-poc/HANDOFF-EXECUTOR.md, 271 functions transpiled, 0 bytes different over 16 MB, entry 0x8C0358BE -- which is exactly the scene FSM this seed pairs to NAOMI 0x0C02AB50',
  statement='maplecast-flycast/tools/render-replica-poc/HANDOFF-EXECUTOR.md (last updated 2026-07-20, branch feat/dataset-exporter, exec commit 4f93dc647) documents a transpile pipeline (lift.py parse, codegen.py per-opcode C mirroring the flycast interpreter, emit_func.py control flow with the delay-slot latch, gen_tick.py batch transpile with re-enterable functions and a global call_addr dispatch over every basic-block address) that runs the whole MvC2 game-logic tick in about 2153 dispatches and diffs ZERO bytes against flycast over the full 16 MB RAM image. Its ENTRY IS 0x8C0358BE, the scene-FSM root -- the same routine this seed identifies as the bsr callee of the DC frame tick loc_8c03589a and pairs with cart 0x0C02AB50. Its verification stack is documented there too: per-leaf byte-exactness with regression constants (RNG seed to 0x92EA332A, nrand fr0 = 0.14776611328125), a flycast --leaf oracle, and the whole-tick diff. Its known open item is finding:executor_sh4_handback_open (the SH4 resumes at a stale PC after the executor hands back).',
  consequence='The SH4 lane has TWO independent routes to a native tick and they should not be confused. Route 1, PROVEN: the hand-written per-opcode transpiler in render-replica-poc, byte-exact on the DC build, driven by an execution trace. Route 2, NEW and unproven: the Ghidra p-code export plus pcode2c.py, which is architecture-neutral and therefore reusable for the cart and for the Steam build. Anyone starting SH4 work should read HANDOFF-EXECUTOR.md before writing a line, and should treat route 2 as owing a gate that route 1 already passed.',
  caveat='Route 1 is byte-exact for the DC build only, from a snapshot at one frame, and it is a game-logic tick, not an emulator. It has never been run against the NAOMI cart.';

